            <ArticleTitle>Atypical manifestation of cat-scratch disease: isolated epigastric pain in an immunocompetent, 12-year-old child.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>669-72</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/ccr3.304</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present a 12-year-old immunocompetent girl with hepato splenic cat-scratch disease (CSD). Her sole inaugural complaint was isolated epigastric pain. She fully recovered, with normalized abdominal CT scan following 2 weeks course of Azythromycin®. CSD should be included in differential diagnosis in children with epigastric pain, especially in those with domestic pets.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
